<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" ?>
<Patch>

  <!--
    Project RimFactory construction drones take their allowed work from the drone station's own mod
    extension rather than from RaceProps.mechEnabledWorkTypes, so they need their own operation.

    This is a player's patch, written and donated by Shin on 1 March 2026 with "Feel free to
    incorporate it into your mod", and shipped here unchanged apart from the success element.

    UNVERIFIED against the mod itself. Project RimFactory is not installed on the machine this was
    written on, so the xpath has not been matched against a real ConstructionDroneStation def. It is
    safe either way: a missed xpath is a silent no-op under <success>Always</success>, and a drone
    that does get the work type is refused by WorkerSkill.FirstBlocker if its race carries no skill
    tracker, rather than reaching the quality roll and throwing there. Worth checking against the
    real def before anyone claims it works.

    Two ways it could miss that are worth knowing. Patches apply before XmlInheritance.Resolve, so
    the xpath only sees nodes the def declares literally in its own file; if the station inherits
    modExtensions from an abstract parent this will not match. And the li class attribute has to be
    the full type name the mod actually writes.

    Load order does not matter. LoadedModManager builds the unified document from every mod's XML
    first and applies all patches afterwards, so this sees Project RimFactory's defs whether it loads
    before or after Simple Improve.
  -->
  <Operation Class="PatchOperationAdd">
    <success>Always</success>
    <xpath>Defs/ThingDef[defName="ConstructionDroneStation"]/modExtensions/li[@Class="ProjectRimFactory.Drones.DefModExtension_DroneStation"]/workTypes</xpath>
    <value>
      <li>WorkType_Improving</li>
    </value>
  </Operation>

</Patch>
